## 1A. Output Discipline Lock (NO NARRATIVE, NO FUTURE-TENSE)
Forbidden in Windsurf responses:
- "Let me…", "I will…", "Next I…", progress narration, apologies, summaries of what was done well.
- Truncation (`...`) of diffs, commands, or outputs.
- Re-explaining prior completed waves.
- Restating constitutional rules.
- Summarizing previous commits.

Allowed response content at phase end (ONLY):
- Evidence file path (under `docs/reports/plans/`)
- Commit hash
- `git show --stat` file list summary (also present inside the evidence file)

---

## 1B. Agent Invocation Lock (FUNCTION-ONLY, NO DUPLICATE SCRIPTS)
When an agent is executed (discovery, validation, enforcement, healing, classification, etc.), it MUST be invoked via a Python function call into the canonical agent implementation.

Hard rules:
- DO NOT create new standalone scripts that duplicate agent behavior or reimplement agent logic.
- CLI/runner entrypoints are allowed ONLY as thin wrappers that:
  - import the canonical agent/module
  - parse args
  - call a single exported Python function
  - contain ZERO business logic beyond wiring/logging/exit codes

If new automation is needed:
- Prefer adding/using a function in the existing agent module (or its canonical helper), then call it.
- Any new script/entrypoint MUST be explicitly justified in the phase plan and MUST demonstrate it delegates to the canonical function without duplicating logic.

Violations are IMMEDIATE FAIL:
- Any new file whose primary purpose is to run an agent by copying logic.
- Any parallel implementation of an existing agent workflow in `tools/`, `scripts/`, `apps_*`, or notebooks.

Evidence requirement (per phase where agents are touched):
- Show the exact call-site (function) used to invoke the agent.
- `rg -n "<agent class/function>"` demonstrating no duplicate runner logic was introduced.

